- Do not commit. Leave the diff for review.

Reference: .local/reports/2026-10-15-appraisal/REPORT.md, Part B.2 stage 9 and Part D item 3."""

TASK2 = """Repository: C:\\Users\\cld-main\\Desktop\\github-projects\\coinpoker-help
Branch: checkpoint/seated-read-mechanism-2-20261002 (work on a new branch or worktree from it).

Goal: implement seven quick-win fixes to the Monitor UI in scripts/dashboard/{index.html, app.js, styles.css}. Add tests in the existing Node-driven harness (scripts/tests/test_companion_ui.py and scripts/tests/test_laya_dashboard_stage2.py).

Context: the Monitor is a no-build, strict-CSP page. Its app.js is a 2,858-line single IIFE that polls /api/state every 250 ms and renders leased, source-bound poker table readings. A 2026-10-15 seven-lens appraisal scored it 5.6/10. The core never shows an unadmitted number, but its operator-facing signals are broken. These seven items touch about 60 lines.

Fixes (verify the line numbers, they may shift):
1. #monitor-empty has class "sr-only" (index.html around line 43), so sighted operators never see the state message. Remove sr-only and keep role="status".
2. styles.css sets `#source-status { color: var(--mint); }`, which paints "Disconnected" and "Session stopped" in the success colour. Remove the rule. In renderSource (app.js around lines 2180-2185), set data-tone okay, warning or danger with the existing status() helper.
3. At 375 px the absolutely positioned seat freshness dot overlaps the seat name. Add about 18px of right padding to `.spatial-seats .seat-select`.
4. Sticky "Stale" label. disconnected() calls clearObservation("stale"). The default parameter persists clearReason, and only a successful admission resets it (app.js around lines 2358-2378 and 2501). So a failed first poll labels never-read fields "Stale" forever. Fix:
   a. Pass "stale" only when a lease was actually active (wasActive).
   b. Reset to "insufficient-context" when a valid snapshot with no observation arrives.
   c. Add a disconnect-first test that asserts "Insufficient context".
5. Make seat and pot validity visible in text. Seat "Last read / Awaiting recheck" reasons are clipped to 1x1 px (`.spatial-seats .seat-amounts .field-reason`), and a provisional CPU-read pot looks exactly like an admitted pot. Fix:
   a. Show a short visible qualifier for provisional and last-read values.
   b. Give each state its own dot shape, not colour alone.
